_flows:"Inflow / outflow",ef_funds_note:"The bar is how much money went into the fund (right) or left it (left). GBTC sold after converting from a trust into an ETF — hence its big outflow.",ef_funds_note2:"The bar is how much money went into the fund (right) or left it (left).",ef_g_defi:"DeFi and wrappers",ef_g_ex:"Exchanges and custodians",ef_g_fund:"ETFs and funds",ef_g_gov:"Governments",ef_g_other:"Other",ef_g_priv:"Private companies",ef_g_pub:"Public companies",ef_h_all:"All",ef_h_found:"{n} holders, {b} together",ef_h_lead:"Known large holders own {b} BTC together — {p} of all bitcoin.",ef_h_more:"Show {n} more",ef_h_none:"Nobody found.",ef_h_note:"The number after the name is how many holders are in the group. Funds are ETFs and closed-end funds; DeFi is wrapped coins like WBTC. Of the 21M cap, about 1M is not mined yet.",ef_h_search:"Find a holder",ef_h_title:"Who holds bitcoin",ef_held:"The funds manage {a} — ≈{c}.",ef_held2:"Since launch the funds have accumulated ≈{c} — {a} at today's price.",ef_how_1:"An ETF is an exchange-traded fund: you buy its share on a regular stock exchange and the fund holds the coin itself. An inflow means the fund bought coins; an outflow means it sold.",ef_how_2:"Funds report once a day after the US market close, so the latest day is yesterday or Friday. There's no trading on weekends.",ef_how_3:"ETF demand vs mining: miners create about 450 BTC a day. If the funds take more, fewer free coins are left on the market.",ef_how_4:"Big holders are based on public reports from companies, funds and governments. That's what's disclosed; exchanges and individuals hold more, but their stacks aren't fully visible.",ef_how_5:"Share is a fund's part of all fund assets for this coin. Premium or discount is how far the fund's share price trades above or below the value of the coins inside — usually a fraction of a percent. A company's average buy price comes from the disclosed cost of its stack.",ef_how_6:"CME positions come from the weekly CFTC report: asset managers are pension and investment funds, hedge funds trade with leverage, dealers are banks and market makers. The net position shows which way big money leans.",ef_in:"In",ef_inflow:"inflow into the funds",ef_last:"Last trading day · {d}",ef_m_note:"Change in holdings over 7 days, from the companies' and funds' public reports and filings.",ef_m_title:"Who added this week",ef_mine_etf_in:"Bought by ETFs",ef_mine_etf_out:"Sold by ETFs",ef_mine_less:"ETFs absorbed {x} of new supply; the rest goes to the market.",ef_mine_more:"ETFs absorbed {x}× more bitcoin than was newly mined: the free supply on the market is shrinking.",ef_mine_new:"Newly mined",ef_mine_sell:"ETFs were net sellers this month: their pressure adds to miners' selling.",ef_mine_title:"ETF demand vs mining over 30 days",ef_mode_c:"Cumulative",ef_mode_d:"Flows",ef_mshare:"share {p}",ef_out:"Out",ef_outflow:"outflow from the funds",ef_p_all:"Since launch",ef_p_d:"Day",ef_p_m:"Month",ef_p_w:"Week",ef_prem:"premium {v}",ef_price:"Price",ef_r_best:"Biggest daily inflow",ef_r_bestm:"Best month",ef_r_note:"Trading days since {d}",ef_r_rundn:"Longest outflow streak",ef_r_runup:"Longest inflow streak",ef_r_title:"Records",ef_r_worst:"Biggest daily outflow",ef_r_worstm:"Worst month",ef_share:"That's {p} of all coins in circulation.",ef_since:"from {d}",ef_src:"Data: CoinMarketCap (ETF flows and assets), bitcointreasuries.net (holders), Binance (prices). Updated hourly.",ef_still:"Funds with no movement: {n}.",ef_streak_in:"Inflows {n} days in a row",ef_streak_out:"Outflows {n} days in a row",ef_sub:"How much money flows into exchange-traded funds and which big holders are buying or selling.",ef_t_title:"Biggest holders",ef_title:"Institutional Flows",ef_upd:"Data as of {t}.",err_invalid_address:"❌ Invalid wallet address.",err_invalid_number:"❌ Invalid number.",err_invoice_failed:"❌ Could not create the invoice. Please try again later.",err_loading_wallet:"❌ Error loading wallet.",err_loading